  "caption_suggestion": "BER versus E_s/N_0 for the corrected-PDP BPSK/long-CP cohort over (a) EVA and (b) ETU; (c) paired 2%-BER threshold penalty of W8A8 versus structured FP32 and PDP-aware Wiener. BER points show the arithmetic mean across three independent training/evaluation seeds, with whiskers indicating sample SD; each seed uses 2000 OFDM slots (640,000 information bits) per channel/SNR. All nine estimators share the same bits, channel taps, and noise within each seed/channel/SNR point. PDP-aware Wiener assumes the known EVA/ETU profile but not instantaneous taps. Oracle rank-one LMMSE uses the true per-realization channel direction as privileged information; it is not a universal BER bound. Curves connect measured SNR points without smoothing. The 2% BER reference is descriptive; sample SD and individual-seed counts are provided in the accompanying source JSON.",
